{"slug": "yeast-raised-waffles", "nyt_id": 11408, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11408-yeast-raised-waffles", "name": "Yeast-Raised Waffles", "author": "Dorie Greenspan", "description": "Dorie Greenspan", "servings": {"text": "About 14 waffles", "min": 14, "max": 14, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup milk, warmed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "milk", "preparation": "warmed", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 packet dry yeast", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "packet dry yeast", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¾ teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 teaspoons pure vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "pure vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 ⅔ cups all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 2.6666666666666665, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "⅔ cup créme fraîche or heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "créme fraîche or heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 stick unsalted butter, melted", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "stick", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "melted", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon kirsch (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "kirsch", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Powdered sugar", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "powdered sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Blend milk and yeast. Let sit 3 minutes. Beat eggs with sugar, salt and vanilla."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Put flour in large bowl; make well in center. Pour milk mixture in center; add egg mixture and crème fraîche. Whisk liquid ingredients together; gradually incorporate flour. Add butter; whisk until batter is smooth. Stir in kirsch. Cover bowl. Let batter rise at room temperature 90 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat waffle iron. Spread batter across grids. Bake 2 minutes, turn and bake until golden. Cool to room temperature."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Dust waffles with sugar. Run under broiler till sugar caramelizes. Serve, cooled."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 228.7, "protein_g": 4.9, "carbohydrates_g": 28.0, "fat_g": 10.5, "saturated_fat_g": 5.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 65.2, "sodium_mg": 152.5, "fiber_g": 0.8, "sugar_g": 9.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course", "side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["all-purpose flour", "fry", "quick", "yeast"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 42}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2002-04-24", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:17:57.129046+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "yellow-and-red-pepper-yin-yang-soup", "nyt_id": 4847, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/4847-yellow-and-red-pepper-yin-yang-soup", "name": "Yellow-and-Red-Pepper Yin-Yang Soup", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "About 1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 yellow bell peppers, stemmed, seeded and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "yellow bell peppers", "preparation": "stemmed, seeded and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 pinches sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "pinch", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 cups chicken or vegetable stock", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken or vegetable stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 red bell peppers, stemmed, seeded and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "red bell peppers", "preparation": "stemmed, seeded and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ dried red chipotle chili, or other smoked, dried chili to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "dried red chipotle chili", "preparation": "or other smoked, dried chili to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 cup heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Kosher salt and freshly ground white pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt and freshly ground white pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon red flying-fish roe or salmon roe for garnish, or brunoise (tiny dice) of red bell pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "red flying-fish roe or salmon roe for garnish", "preparation": "or brunoise (tiny dice) of red bell pepper", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon sevruga caviar for garnish, or brunoise of yellow bell pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sevruga caviar for garnish", "preparation": "or brunoise of yellow bell pepper", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Chopped chives for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chopped chives for garnish", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a small saucepan, combine the yellow peppers, cumin, 1 pinch of the sugar and 2 cups of the stock. In another small saucepan, combine the red peppers, chipotle, remaining pinch sugar and remaining 2 cups stock. Place both pans over medium heat, bring to a boil, reduce the heat and simmer, uncovered, until the peppers are very tender, about 25 minutes. Remove both pans from the heat and allow to cool."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Transfer the yellow-pepper mixture to a blender and blend until smooth. Strain through a fine-mesh sieve back into the pan, pressing the solids with the back of a spoon to extract as much liquid as possible. Discard the solids. Repeat the process with red-pepper mixture."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Place both pans over medium-low heat and stir ½ cup cream into each saucepan. Season to taste with salt and pepper; do not boil."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Warm 6 wide soup bowls. Using 4 layers of aluminum foil, fashion a divider that will fit securely in bowls, dividing each in half. Place divider in one bowl. Pour ½ cup yellow soup into a cup with a spout. Pour ½ cup red soup into another cup with a spout. Simultaneously pour each soup into separate halves of bowl. Carefully remove divider. Garnish yellow half of the soup with ½ teaspoon red caviar (or brunoise of red pepper). Garnish red half with ½ teaspoon sevruga caviar (or brunoise of yellow pepper). Sprinkle with chives. Repeat with all bowls and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 249.2, "protein_g": 7.5, "carbohydrates_g": 19.6, "fat_g": 16.8, "saturated_fat_g": 9.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.5, "cholesterol_mg": 49.6, "sodium_mg": 865.8, "fiber_g": 3.4, "sugar_g": 6.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": ["lunch"], "occasion": [], "other": ["bell pepper", "boil", "caviar", "great leftovers", "soup"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1999-09-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T06:59:51.223724+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
